ducts comprising metadata libraries, covering television, sports, movies, digital-first, and celebrities; personalized content discovery, natural language voice, and insights; direct-to-consumer retail TiVo DVR subscriptions; and technical support operations. In addition, it offers home, mobile audio, and DTS post-processing audio solutions; Connected Car solutions, such as HD radio, a digital terrestrial broadcast system and DTS autostage, an automotive infotainment platform; and media platform, including TiVo OS, TiVo OS for TV devices, TiVo OS for Car, and TiVo OS, as well as TV viewership data and advertising monetization solutions. The company was incorporated in 2019 and is headquartered in San Jose, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jon E. Kirchner CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $327K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers. Stock-based compensation of $30K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Xperi Inc. is a micro-cap technology business with a $296M market cap on $448M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -26% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $6M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -14.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 2.0% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 4.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 17% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 62% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Precision Trading with Xperi Inc. (XPER) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/141/Precision_Trading_with_Xperi_Inc._XPER_Risk_Zones_110826011401_1794161641.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794161641.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Xperi (XPER) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/xperi-xper-q3-2026-earni